{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25218778",
      "title": "Key Feature: Server-side (Pre-) Rendering of Pages",
      "lectureOrder": 417,
      "videoOrder": 384,
      "sourceHash": "519acf2db21dc2533e50dfbc0bc7cdc597a125510dbc0e2e4348a75793e7f8ba",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.856,
          "end": 3.31,
          "en": "So let's have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.31,
          "end": 6.92,
          "en": "at the NextJS key features and benefits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.92,
          "end": 10.19,
          "en": "And whilst we go through them, it will also become clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.19,
          "end": 15.19,
          "en": "why I like to call NextJS a full stack framework as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.59,
          "end": 20.59,
          "en": "I would say the most important key feature NextJS adds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.01,
          "end": 24.86,
          "en": "is the built-in server-side rendering support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.86,
          "end": 26.2,
          "en": "Now in case it's not clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.2,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "what server-side rendering means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 32.96,
          "en": "server-side rendering is all about preparing the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.96,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "of a page on the server instead of on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 40.4,
          "en": "If you take a standard React application built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.4,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "with just React, then if you inspect the source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 48.55,
          "en": "of a loaded React page, you will notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.55,
          "end": 51.04,
          "en": "that the page is actually pretty empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.04,
          "end": 52.38,
          "en": "right from the start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.38,
          "end": 55.88,
          "en": "You only have a basic HTML skeleton there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.88,
          "end": 58.32,
          "en": "and then some entry point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.32,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "some div with an idea route typically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "into which the React app is loaded and rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 68.67,
          "en": "But all of that rendering, is done by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.67,
          "end": 72.56,
          "en": "And since React is a client side, JavaScript library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.56,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "all that rendering happens on the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 78.28,
          "en": "so in the browsers of your users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.28,
          "end": 80.95,
          "en": "it's not happening on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.95,
          "end": 84.74,
          "en": "And as a result, the actual HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.74,
          "end": 87.58,
          "en": "which is sent from the server to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.58,
          "end": 90.883,
          "en": "when a user visits your page is pretty empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.81,
          "end": 95.1,
          "en": "Now, that is not necessarily a big problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.1,
          "end": 98.93,
          "en": "It depends on what you're building, but it can be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.93,
          "end": 101.78,
          "en": "Because for example, if your page also,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.78,
          "end": 103.97999999999999,
          "en": "fetches some data from a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 105.19,
          "en": "that should be displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.19,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "like a list of meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 107.89,
          "en": "as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.89,
          "end": 111.62,
          "en": "then the user might initially see some loading state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.62,
          "end": 114.72999999999999,
          "en": "a flickering page for a fraction of a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.72999999999999,
          "end": 118.17,
          "en": "whilst the request is on its way, fetching the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.17,
          "end": 120.79,
          "en": "because data fetching only begins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.79,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "once the JavaScript code executed on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 126.14,
          "en": "And then we still have to wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.14,
          "end": 128.833,
          "en": "for the response of that outgoing request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.98,
          "end": 132.99,
          "en": "Simply because the page which we requested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 135.91,
          "en": "did not yet contain that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.91,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "Now, again, that is not necessarily a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 141.82,
          "en": "but of course it might not be the user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.82,
          "end": 143.64,
          "en": "you want to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 145.64,
          "en": "Now it can also be a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.64,
          "end": 149.11,
          "en": "if search engine optimization matters to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.11,
          "end": 152.04,
          "en": "Now, this does not matter for all pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.04,
          "end": 154.99,
          "en": "If you have a administration dashboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.99,
          "end": 157.49,
          "en": "which is only reached by logging in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.49,
          "end": 159.45,
          "en": "then search engine optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.45,
          "end": 160.49099999999999,
          "en": "does not matter there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.49099999999999,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "because search engines will never see that dashboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.18,
          "en": "It's highly user specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.18,
          "end": 168.81,
          "en": "and you need to log in any ways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.81,
          "end": 171.62,
          "en": "but if you have a public facing page with a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.62,
          "end": 175.04,
          "en": "of content that should be found through search engines,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.04,
          "end": 178.52,
          "en": "then of course, search engine optimization does matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.52,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "So for example, here, where we got this list of meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 184.46,
          "en": "we see those meetups as a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.46,
          "end": 188.84,
          "en": "but the search engine crawlers will actually only see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.84,
          "end": 191.65,
          "en": "that initially empty HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.65,
          "end": 193.49,
          "en": "which we're getting from a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.49,
          "end": 197.88,
          "en": "So, that content is not picked up by search engine crawlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.88,
          "end": 200.8,
          "en": "and that can be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.8,
          "end": 203.77,
          "en": "And that's where a server-side rendering could help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.77,
          "end": 207.77,
          "en": "If that page would be pre-rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.77,
          "end": 211.41,
          "en": "if that data fetching somehow could be done on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 213.55,
          "en": "when the request hits that server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.55,
          "end": 216.47,
          "en": "and then the finished page would be served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.47,
          "end": 219.82,
          "en": "to our users and to the search engine crawlers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.82,
          "end": 223.42000000000002,
          "en": "then users would not have that flickering loading state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.42000000000002,
          "end": 227.28,
          "en": "and search engines would see our page content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.28,
          "end": 229.93,
          "en": "And that's the problem server-side rendering solves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.93,
          "end": 233.27,
          "en": "It allows us to pre-render React pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.27,
          "end": 236.77,
          "en": "React components on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.77,
          "end": 240.66,
          "en": "Now ReactJS actually has built-in features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 240.66,
          "end": 243.51,
          "en": "that allow you to add server-side rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.51,
          "end": 245.41,
          "en": "but it can be tricky to get that right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.41,
          "end": 248.9,
          "en": "And it requires extra setup from your side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.9,
          "end": 252.4,
          "en": "With NextJS, that becomes way easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.4,
          "end": 256.49,
          "en": "because NextJS has built-in server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.49,
          "end": 260.31,
          "en": "It automatically pre renders your pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.31,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "and that means that with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.35,
          "en": "if you build a standard NextJS app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 268.43,
          "en": "without any extra setup from your side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 268.43,
          "end": 270,
          "en": "if you visit such a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270,
          "end": 274.73,
          "en": "it was pre-rendered on the server by default out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.73,
          "end": 277.118,
          "en": "And that means that it's great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.118,
          "end": 278.34000000000003,
          "en": "for a search engine optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.34000000000003,
          "end": 282.1,
          "en": "because search engines see what our users see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.1,
          "end": 286.57,
          "en": "and our users also have a better initial load experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.57,
          "end": 289.74,
          "en": "because they don't have that initial flickering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.74,
          "end": 293.47,
          "en": "If we inspect the source code of a NextJS page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.47,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "it's half a page in the NextJS app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 297.44,
          "en": "then we see that there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.44,
          "end": 300.7,
          "en": "it's not just an empty HTML skeleton,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.7,
          "end": 304.61,
          "en": "but instead all the content is already there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.61,
          "end": 308.91,
          "en": "in that HTML page, which we got back from the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 308.91,
          "end": 311.789,
          "en": "Now it is worth noting that with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 311.789,
          "end": 315.46,
          "en": "after this initial load offered as initial request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.46,
          "end": 319.12,
          "en": "we still get a standard React app running in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 319.12,
          "end": 322.51,
          "en": "a standard single page application even,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.51,
          "end": 325.72,
          "en": "subsequent navigation actions by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.72,
          "end": 329.02,
          "en": "So when the user then browses our page and navigates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 329.02,
          "end": 332.96,
          "en": "around, those actions are all handled by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 332.96,
          "end": 337.27,
          "en": "in the browser to have this fast interactive user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.27,
          "end": 340.15999999999997,
          "en": "which we typically wanna offer with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.15999999999997,
          "end": 341.40999999999997,
          "en": "which was one of the reasons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.40999999999997,
          "end": 343.94,
          "en": "why you would use React typically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.94,
          "end": 346.86,
          "en": "So we still get that but for the initial load,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.86,
          "end": 349.58,
          "en": "we have that pre-rendered page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 349.58,
          "end": 351.46,
          "en": "And that in the end, means that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 351.46,
          "end": 353.49,
          "en": "client site and server-side code is kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 353.49,
          "end": 357.33,
          "en": "of blended together with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 357.33,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "And of course in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 362.99,
          "en": "you are going to learn how things are blending together,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 362.99,
          "end": 365.56,
          "en": "how you can write code that runs on a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 365.56,
          "end": 368.59,
          "en": "and how you can write code that runs on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 368.59,
          "end": 371.83,
          "en": "You are of course, going to learn all about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 371.83,
          "end": 374.61,
          "en": "And this is therefore, of the major features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 374.61,
          "end": 376.59,
          "en": "that makes up NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 376.59,
          "end": 379.15,
          "en": "This built-in server-side rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.15,
          "end": 384.15,
          "en": "which on its own probably would already be a strong benefit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 384.24,
          "end": 388.88,
          "en": "or a strong reason for why you might want to use NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 388.88,
          "end": 393.37,
          "en": "for building your React projects instead of just ReactJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.37,
          "end": 396.063,
          "en": "But it's not the only key feature.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
